# Generated from: specs/19-deliver-transactional-email-with-observable-retry-and-resend/requirements.md
Feature: Deliver transactional email with observable retry and resend
  As a volunteer and coordinator
  I want private scheduling links delivered reliably with visible failure handling
  So that the workflow does not depend on copying raw URLs by hand

  @SCN001
  Scenario Outline: Committed workflow creates automatic delivery
    Given a <event> transition and notification intent can commit atomically
    When the transition succeeds and the worker processes its intent
    Then Resend receives one encoded plain-text and HTML message with group-local commitment context
    And any private link material exists only transiently while its hash persists
    And provider outcome commits independently from workflow state

    Examples:
      | event                 |
      | request receipt       |
      | assignment access     |
      | access recovery       |
      | schedule correction   |
      | cancellation          |
      | deactivation          |

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Transient failure follows bounded idempotent retry
    Given Resend returns a transient failure for a due message
    When the in-process worker runs through its retry policy
    Then attempts occur at 0, 1, 5, 30, and 120 minutes at most
    And identical in-memory submissions reuse one Resend idempotency key
    And fresh secret material uses a new attempt and key after abandoned work
    And the fifth failure becomes final without another workflow transition

  @SCN003
  Scenario: Provider acceptance and delivery remain distinct
    Given Resend accepts a message and returns a provider message ID
    When no webhook has arrived
    Then the coordinator sees Accepted by email service
    When a valid signed delivered webhook arrives
    Then the coordinator sees Delivered to mail server
    And the application does not claim that the volunteer read the message

  @SCN004
  Scenario Outline: Signed terminal webhook overrides accepted state
    Given an accepted message has provider ID and a verified <event> webhook arrives
    When the event is processed twice or out of order with a delivered event
    Then one webhook receipt is stored
    And visible state remains <state>
    And no raw webhook body or recipient is persisted or logged

    Examples:
      | event            | state                   |
      | email.bounced    | Bounced                 |
      | email.complained | Recipient reported spam |

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Provider failure cannot roll back scheduling
    Given a scheduling transition and notification intent committed
    When Resend times out or permanently rejects the message
    Then schedule, request, assignment, capability, and audit state remain committed
    And notification state alone becomes retrying or not sent
    And the coordinator can request another copy without repeating the workflow transition

  @SCN006
  Scenario: Coordinator resend is visible and audited
    Given a delivery failed or a volunteer asks for another copy
    When an allowlisted coordinator requests resend or access reissue
    Then a deduplicated new intent receives its own retry budget
    And the request is audited without destination, credentials, or raw links
    And issue 18 normal versus revoke-now access semantics are preserved
